command-description-colorcontrol-color =
    Sets the color applied to the targeted layers and optionally how it's applied (Replace or Multiply). Omit the color to clear it.
command-description-colorcontrol-shader =
    Sets the shader applied to the targeted layers, e.g. unshaded. Omit the shader to clear it.
command-description-colorcontrol-targets =
    Sets which layer groups are affected (Body, Clothing, Held, All, None). Ignored while manual layers are set.
command-description-colorcontrol-addlayer =
    Adds a layer to the manually targeted layers by key and/or index. Use _ to skip the key.
command-description-colorcontrol-removelayer =
    Removes a layer from the manually targeted layers by key and/or index. Use _ to skip the key.
command-description-colorcontrol-clearlayers =
    Clears all manually targeted layers, falling back to the target groups.
command-description-colorcontrol-layer =
    Sets the color, mode and shader override for a layer key. Use _ to skip values, or give no values to remove the override.
command-description-colorcontrol-clearoverrides =
    Removes all per-layer overrides.
command-description-colorcontrol-ignoreshader =
    Adds a shader to (or with false, removes it from) the shaders whose layers are never touched.
command-description-colorcontrol-reset =
    Removes color control from the entity, restoring its original colors and shaders.
